cription":"Previously reported settlements with government authorities include a May 2015 guilty plea to one federal antitrust violation. DOL exemptions were granted without a stated grant date; January 2017 starts the ten-year disqualification period, not the plea or exemption action. A remaining governmental inquiry is separately disclosed."},{"kind":"CURRENT_REGULATORY_ACTION","subject":"Firm FX-related South Africa matter","event_dates":[],"reported_context_times":[],"status":"CURRENTLY_PENDING","evidence":[{"unit_id":"sha256:622b0eebd9155bdacb77f07779b6e5046a566330559e2ae97a527c65b1d1a8fa","kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":10172},{"unit_id":"sha256:622b0eebd9155bdacb77f07779b6e5046a566330559e2ae97a527c65b1d1a8fa","kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":10175}],"description":"Only remaining FX-related governmental inquiry is the South Africa Competition Commission matter, currently pending before the South Africa Competition Tribunal; read across the page break. No action date is supplied."},{"kind":"PRIVATE_OR_INTERNAL_ACTION","subject":"Firm FX-related foreign civil proceedings","event_dates":["2025-12"],"reported_context_times":[],"status":"PRIVATE_CASES_REMAIN; ISRAEL_SETTLEMENT_AWAITING_APPROVAL","evidence":[{"unit_id":"sha256:622b0eebd9155bdacb77f07779b6e5046a566330559e2ae97a527c65b1d1a8fa","kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":10176}],"description":"Individual/putative class actions remain outside the U.S. In December 2025 the U.K. Supreme Court confirmed denial of opt-out class certification. Israel has a settlement in principle subject to court approval. These civil steps do not establish government investigations."},{"kind":"PRIVATE_OR_INTERNAL_ACTION","subject":"Interchange damages class action","event_dates":["2018-09"],"reported_context_times":[],"status":"PRIVATE_DAMAGES_CLASS_SETTLED","evidence":[{"unit_id":"sha256:622b0eebd9155bdacb77f07779b6e5046a566330559e2ae97a527c65b1d1a8fa","kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":10178}],"description":"Parties settled the class action seeking monetary relief in September 2018. This does not close the separate injunctive class action or remaining merchant opt-out actions."},{"kind":"PRIVATE_OR_INTERNAL_ACTION","subject":"Interchange injunctive class action","event_dates":["2024-06","2025-11"],"reported_context_times":[],"status":"CONTINUES; AMENDED_SETTLEMENT_SUBMITTED","evidence":[{"unit_id":"sha256:622b0eebd9155bdacb77f07779b6e5046a566330559e2ae97a527c65b1d1a8fa","kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":10178}],"description":"Eastern District of New York denied preliminary settlement approval in June 2024. Parties reached a superseding amended settlement and submitted it for court approval in November 2025. Approval or closure is not asserted."},{"kind":"PRIVATE_OR_INTERNAL_ACTION","subject":"Firm and other defendants: merchant opt-out interchange claims","event_dates":["2026-04"],"reported_context_times":[],"status":"REMAINING_CLAIMS_PENDING; TRIAL_SCHEDULED","evidence":[{"unit_id":"sha256:622b0eebd9155bdacb77f07779b6e5046a566330559e2ae97a527c65b1d1a8fa","kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":10179}],"description":"Settlements cover opt-out merchants representing over 90% of combined card-sales volume, not all claims. Southern District of New York scheduled several merchants claims for trial beginning April 2026; this is a planned action date, not a completed trial or reporting period."},{"kind":"REPORTED_REGULATORY_PROCESS","subject":"Firm response to LIBOR/EURIBOR governmental inquiries","event_dates":[],"reported_context_times":[],"status":"HISTORICAL_RESPONSE; ONGOING_INQUIRIES_UNESTABLISHED","evidence":[{"unit_id":"sha256:622b0eebd9155bdacb77f07779b6e5046a566330559e2ae97a527c65b1d1a8fa","kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":10180}],"description":"Firm has responded to inquiries from various governmental agencies/entities worldwide about benchmark rates. Recipient is the Firm; investigated targets, response dates and continuing inquiry status are not supplied. The specific EURIBOR enforcement appeal is separately retained."},{"kind":"CURRENT_REGULATORY_ACTION","subject":"Firm and other banks: EURIBOR European antitrust enforcement","event_dates":["2016-12","2023-12","2024-03","2026-01"],"reported_context_times":[],"status":"ENFORCEMENT_DECISION_UNDER_APPEAL; JUDGMENT_RESERVED","evidence":[{"unit_id":"sha256:622b0eebd9155bdacb77f07779b6e5046a566330559e2ae97a527c65b1d1a8fa","kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":10180},{"unit_id":"sha256:622b0eebd9155bdacb77f07779b6e5046a566330559e2ae97a527c65b1d1a8fa","kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":10181}],"description":"European Commission infringement decision: December 2016. General Court annulled but re-imposed an identical fine: December 2023. Firm appealed to Court of Justice: March 2024. That court held a hearing and reserved judgment: January 2026. Annulment did not eliminate the fine; no new investigation is inferred."},{"kind":"PRIVATE_OR_INTERNAL_ACTION","subject":"Firm and other banks: U.S. dollar LIBOR civil claims","event_dates":["2025-09"],"reported_context_times":[],"status":"DISMISSED_WITH_PREJUDICE; PLAINTIFFS_APPEAL","evidence":[{"unit_id":"sha256:622b0eebd9155bdacb77f07779b6e5046a566330559e2ae97a527c65b1d1a8fa","kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":10182}],"description":"Southern District of New York granted defendants summary judgment, decertified the class and dismissed all remaining U.S. dollar LIBOR claims in September 2025. Plaintiffs appealed, without a stated appeal date. This private litigation is distinct from governmental benchmark inquiries."},{"kind":"PRIVATE_OR_INTERNAL_ACTION","subject":"Firm Russian payment litigation and asset measures","event_dates":[],"reported_context_times":[],"status":"JUDGMENTS; APPEALS_AND_FREEZES","evidence":[{"unit_id":"sha256:622b0eebd9155bdacb77f07779b6e5046a566330559e2ae97a527c65b1d1a8fa","kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":10183},{"unit_id":"sha256:622b0eebd9155bdacb77f07779b6e5046a566330559e2ae97a527c65b1d1a8fa","kind":"V